<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Basra is a port city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, founded around 636 as a garrison town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>. It became a major commercial and intellectual centre of the early Islamic world. In the 1770s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan Zand</a>'s forces besieged and captured it, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a>'s main military ventures.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basra.jpg" alt="Basra" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Basra city.jpg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basra_city.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
